.TH FOLD 5
.SH NAME
fold \- folded part file
.SH DESCRIPTION
A fold file holds one or more parts.
Each part is its flat blank, divided into faces along the edges of the
bend zones, with a map for each face from flat coordinates
(x, y, z), z in [\-t, 0], to 3D.
A slab is mapped by a rotation and a translation; a bend zone (a
rectangle across the full width) is wrapped round the bend axis of its
parent slab.
The top face, z = 0, is the reference face.
One record per line, \- for no face:
.PP
.RS
.nf
part NAME
t T
place R00 R01 R02 R10 R11 R12 R20 R21 R22 TX TY TZ
colour NAME R G B ROUGHNESS
map I rigid R00 ... R22 TX TY TZ
map I bend PARENT QX QY MX MY BA ANGLE R
face I MAP
vertex I X Y
edge I V0 V1 LEFT RIGHT [arc CX CY]
hole FACE CX CY R [csink RC H top|bottom]
end
.fi
.RE
.PP
Indices start at 0 for each kind of record.
The colour is optional, its values from 0 to 1.
Arcs run counterclockwise from V0 to V1; the face on the left of an
edge is bounded counterclockwise.
A bend zone is BA wide and begins on the line through (QX, QY)
perpendicular to (MX, MY), the unit vector into the zone.
.SH SEE ALSO
smfold(1), place(1), sm(5)
